Wait no! This won't work because `appendChild` will detach the existing nodes from their current location before appending them to the fragment. But I'm also calling `todoList.innerHTML = ''` after. If I've already moved the nodes to the fragment, they're no longer children of todoList, so innerHTML would clear nothing.

But wait, `fragment.appendChild(li)` when `li` is already in the DOM will first remove it, then add it to the fragment. So the existing elements are detached from the todoList. Then when I do `todoList.innerHTML = ''` it clears any remaining children (should be none if I've processed all). Then `todoList.appendChild(fragment)` puts them back.

The key question: does moving a DOM element to a fragment and then back preserve its identity? Yes! The element object itself is the same, references to it remain valid. Cypress holds a reference to the element, and as long as the element isn't destroyed and recreated, it remains valid
